# Board Game journal

Edit entries directly in `index.html`, inside `<article id="journal">`.
No Markdown conversion, build, or server-side app is needed. Keep newer entries
above older entries; use `<h2>` for dates and `<p>` for paragraphs.

The page shares `../Chord Organ/styles.css` and `../Chord Organ/journal.js`:
white background, centered 700px column, 14pt Times New Roman body, 2em paragraph
indents, bold 16pt dates, italic 12pt captions, Main Menu at top left, and
Jump to Oldest at bottom right. Both controls use underlined 16pt Times New Roman.

Images use `<figure>`, `<img>`, and `<figcaption>`. Inline image styles allow
individual width and height limits; keep `height: auto` for natural proportions.
`images/` is the single image folder for the journal and contains browser-friendly JPEGs.
The initial November 11, 2026 date is a collection date, not a photo timestamp.

The old simulator is no longer loaded. Its styles, JavaScript, data, and Python
helpers are unused by the journal and retained separately in this folder.
